WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.737
This slide gives us a simple workflow for building
SQL logic Step

00:00:05.763 --> 00:00:09.708
one is to define the rule in plain language Do not
start

00:00:09.733 --> 00:00:14.301
with SQL yet Step two is to inspect the fields
involved and

00:00:14.327 --> 00:00:19.145
ask whether any of them can contain null values Step
three is

00:00:19.171 --> 00:00:26.220
to group related conditions This is where
parentheses become very important Step

00:00:26.246 --> 00:00:30.487
four is to decide the order of your case conditions
Remember that

00:00:30.513 --> 00:00:35.725
the first matching case branch wins Step five is to
test unusual

00:00:35.751 --> 00:00:43.063
records including null values blank text zero values
and exact boundaries Finally

00:00:43.308 --> 00:00:48.038
validate the result against the original rule The
main idea is simple

00:00:48.335 --> 00:00:53.000
reason first then write the SQL A clear rule usually
leads to

00:00:53.013 --> 00:00:53.812
clearer code
